z3-4.3.1's ARM64 build does not respect -t 1 the way every other platform's
z3-4.3 build does here: check-sat never returns 'unknown' under the timeout
(confirmed via CI run 35677246677), unlike the identical workload on
macos-arm64/macos-x64/linux-x64/windows. Consistent with already-tracked,
unrelated ARM64-specific z3-4.3.1 defects (issues #101, #102 -- wrong
verdicts/truncated output, and hangs on get-info respectively) rather than a
flaw in this script or in jSMTLIB's -t/-T handling itself. Skip rather than
weaken the timeout-mechanism assertion for every other platform to
accommodate this one broken binary.
